WEBVTT

00:00:00.873 --> 00:00:02.686
<v><b>Annabel:</b></v> Hello. I’m Annabel.

00:00:02.728 --> 00:00:03.980
<v><b>Peter:</b></v> And I’m Peter.

00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:05.905
<v><b>Expert:</b></v> Hi there, Annabel and Peter.

00:00:05.955 --> 00:00:07.350
What’s your problem?

00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:11.514
<v><b>Annabel:</b></v> We’ve got a son, Jamie, and he’s twenty-five.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:13.080
He’s a chef.

00:00:13.301 --> 00:00:15.923
<v><b>Peter:</b></v> But he still lives with us because he says

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:20.300
it’s too expensive to rent a flat and he doesn’t earn enough money.

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:26.482
<v><b>Annabel:</b></v> He gives us some money every month for bills – not much, but a bit – and,

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:31.939
you know, it’s nice to have him at home, but we think he needs to be more independent.

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:33.397
<v><b>Peter:</b></v> Yes, absolutely.

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:36.179
<v><b>Annabel:</b></v> But last week he told us that

00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:40.174
he’s planning a two-week holiday to Mexico with his friends.

00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:47.287
I mean, it’s true that he works full-time and we know he needs a break, but we really think…

00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:51.050
<v><b>Peter:</b></v> Yes, we don’t think he should go on an expensive holiday when

00:00:51.075 --> 00:00:53.010
he doesn’t give us much money.

00:00:53.498 --> 00:00:58.019
We think he should save his money so that he can get his own place to live.

00:00:58.086 --> 00:01:00.726
Should we tell him that he can’t go to Mexico?